# .dockerignore — keep the build context small and leak-free.
#
# Both Dockerfiles COPY an explicit list of root-level modules, so anything
# excluded here is build context that can never reach an image. Two consequences
# worth stating: (1) excluding a file that a COPY references is a hard build
# failure, so the module names below were checked against both COPY lists; (2)
# the forensic artefacts that live in this working tree are excluded on purpose
# — .gitignore already refuses to commit them because they contain operator
# usernames, roles, MFA state, commands and device fingerprints, and baking a
# developer's ledger into an image would copy exactly that data somewhere it was
# never meant to go.
#
# Verified against this repository as it stands: the only archive/binary
# payloads present are build/SecureGuard/base_library.zip (1.3 MB, PyInstaller
# intermediate) and dist/SecureGuard.exe (84 MB). There are currently NO vendored
# OpenGL DLLs or wheel archives anywhere in the tree — the Windows/OpenGL DLLs
# the launcher used to ship are gone. The *.dll / *.whl / *.lib patterns below
# are therefore a guard against them being reintroduced, not a description of
# the current tree. Nothing the Linux runtime needs comes from this repo: Mesa
# and the GLX/EGL stack are installed from apt in Dockerfile.dashboard.

# --- Version control and agent scratch space --------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.opencode/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Build outputs -----------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.spec
# Windows-only launchers; the container uses python main_qt.py directly.
*.bat
*.cmd

# --- Runtime state (must come from the volume, never from the image) ---------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.jsonl
risk_thresholds.json
.secureguard/
evidence_archive/
logs/

# --- Secrets: never let a local key or .env reach an image layer --------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt

# --- Vendored native payloads (see note above) -------------------------------
*.dll
*.whl
*.lib
*.a
*.pyd
*.dylib
*.so
archive/
vendor/
vendored/
third_party/

# --- Docs and tests: not needed at runtime -----------------------------------
docs/
tests/
test_*.py
conftest.py
demo.py
create_shortcut_qt.py
README.md
*.md

# --- OS cruft ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
